WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Good to have you on Tesla Short's time, daily, episode 514.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.720
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.840
Today is June 18th, 2026.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.060
Lots happening across deliveries, FSD, and the stock today.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:20.840
Tesla's FSD update will remember owners parking preferences and reduce repeated manual inputs

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.120
during daily drives.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.860
Tesla filed for regulatory approval of supervised, full self-driving in Taiwan.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.760
The application targets the supervised version for review in a new major Asian market.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.960
This follows prior supervised rollouts in other regions and requires full regulator sign

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.480
off before any launch.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.720
Approval would expand the geographic footprint of the current supervised stack.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.440
The filing reflects ongoing efforts to secure business clearances in additional markets.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.280
Regulators will now examine the submission in detail from market expansion efforts

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.520
to the software features that will actually run in those markets.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:10.080
Upcoming FSD releases will let owners recall familiar parking spots and habits without repeated inputs.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.580
Grok voice integration is also planned for the supervised stack.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:21.020
The changes aim to cut manual steps on daily drives while staying within the supervised framework.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.780
Owners can expect the updates in a future software branch.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.660
Development ties into broader improvements for the current supervised system.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:35.680
While the software improves, capital allocation is shifting away from vehicles entirely.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:42.080
Tesla's capital expenditure guidance now allocates the majority of the $25 billion plan

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.660
toward AI infrastructure and robotics programs.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:51.060
The shift moves resources away from traditional vehicle manufacturing lines.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.400
The plan reflects internal prioritization of autonomy and humanoid development.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:01.680
Investors are evaluating how the reallocation affects near-term vehicle margins.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.880
Future earnings updates will detail the split between hardware and software spending.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:12.940
Capital questions lead directly into questions about data integrity behind autonomy claims.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:20.160
Investigators claim Tesla submitted altered safety statistics during European FSD approval reviews.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.060
The discrepancies involve collision and intervention rates that differ from internal logs.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.400
If confirmed, the findings can trigger re-examination of existing approvals and new data requirements.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.080
Tesla has not yet issued a public response to the specific allegations.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:43.940
Data questions aside, real-world efficiency comparisons are emerging between Tesla and rivals.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:50.800
EPA documents show the Rivian R2 performance matches the model Y in energy consumption,

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.820
despite being roughly 500 pounds heavier.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:03:00.240
The result comes from differences in aerodynamics, motor calibration, and battery management.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:05.100
Both vehicles post identical consumption figures under the same test cycle.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:10.180
The comparison highlights how weight alone does not determine efficiency outcomes.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.440
Future production versions will confirm whether the numbers hold in real-world use.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.940
Vehicle efficiency numbers rarely line up so cleanly across different architectures.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:28.220
The Rivian R2 posting identical consumption to the model Y while carrying several hundred extra pounds

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:33.680
points to how aero, motor mapping, and thermal systems can offset mass penalties.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.360
The result is not an accident of testing conditions,

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.680
but a reminder that curb weight is only one variable among many that determine real-world energy use.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.800
When two vehicles reach the same EPA figure through different design choices,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.960
buyers and fleet operators gain more flexibility in selecting body styles or payload ratings

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.080
without immediate efficiency trade-offs.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.980
That flexibility matters for margins because it widens the set of configurations

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.780
that still meet customer range expectations.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.960
It also reduces the pressure to chase every last kilogram of weight reduction at the expense of

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:17.360
interior space or feature content. Efficiency insights connect to how companies study rivals hardware

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:24.140
costs. Tesla and Ford disassembled Chinese market EVs to study component choices and cost structures.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.880
Engineers noted specific design decisions that lowered production expenses.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.780
The findings highlighted differences in battery integration and assembly methods.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.940
Both companies are applying similar cost analysis approaches to their own programs.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:43.660
The work shows how competitive benchmarking influences component sourcing.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:50.200
Hardware benchmarking gives way to the first regulatory numbers on Tesla's own next-generation vehicle.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:56.040
EPA filings list the CyberCab's curb weight, power output, and estimated range.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.640
The vehicle sits several hundred pounds below the latest current Model 3.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:05.360
Power and range figures align with earlier prototype disclosures.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.820
The data provides the first regulatory benchmark for production planning.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.780
Fleet operators will use the numbers to model energy and payload requirements.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:21.020
A driver activated FSD during a sudden health event and reached help through the Tesla app.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:27.420
The combination of supervised autonomy and remote connectivity allowed the vehicle to continue safely.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.900
First responders later credited the features for shortening response time.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:37.560
The incident shows how current supervised tools can function in unplanned situations.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:44.720
Regulators in the Netherlands counted roughly 40,000 vehicles running Tesla's supervised FSD package.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.800
The figure comes from vehicle registration and software telemetry data.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:54.940
Officials are monitoring usage patterns ahead of any future policy changes.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.560
Android users will soon receive real-time charging status updates similar to iOS live activities.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.540
The feature displays progress without opening the full app.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:09.880
Development closes a long-standing parity gap between platforms.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:17.100
Tesla's combination of app-based access, location tracking, and software locks makes unauthorized

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:22.660
starts difficult. Owners report lower-theft concerns compared with conventional vehicles.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:27.880
The system requires authenticated phone keys or account credentials for operation.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.700
Law enforcement data cited in the report shows fewer successful thefts.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.840
The design reduces the value of physical key duplication attempts.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:42.600
Reports indicate that the layered security approach has contributed to measurable drops in

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:49.200
reported incidents for Tesla vehicles. A household driving two Tesla's 500 miles weekly reported

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:55.640
lower monthly electricity costs than expected. The bills reflected home charging at standard

00:06:55.640 --> 00:07:01.980
residential rates. The couple compared the figures against prior gasoline expenses for similar mileage.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:08.020
The outcome shows how home charging economics vary by utility pricing and driving patterns.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.220
No public charging network costs were included in the calculation.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:17.660
The experience highlighted how consistent residential rates can produce predictable weekly

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:23.680
expenses for high mileage households. Polestar UK shifted away from Tesla style,

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:30.160
direct sales toward a hybrid retail model. The change includes physical showrooms and test drive

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:36.020
centers in key cities. Management cited customer preference for in-person evaluation before

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:41.480
purchase. The revised approach aims to increase test drive volume and brand visibility.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.700
Early results will be tracked through regional registration data.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.980
The pivot reflects an effort to address buyer hesitation observed in markets where online only

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:58.620
channels dominate. Elon Musk exercised additional options and increased his Tesla shareholding.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:04.300
The transaction added to an already substantial position valued at over $100 billion.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:10.220
Timing coincides with ongoing speculation about potential corporate combinations.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:16.780
The filing shows continued personal capital commitment to the company. Investors are watching for

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:22.840
any follow-on statements on strategic direction. The increased stake comes amid broader market

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:29.240
discussion of long-term alignment between Tesla and related ventures. Patent images reveal

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:36.140
Lucid's planned cosmos SUV design. The vehicle targets the same size class as the Model Y.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:41.600
Styling cues and proportions suggest a direct competitor for the Australian market.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.900
The accidental release gives early insight into Lucid's next product timing.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:52.300
Production plans remain subject to final regulatory and supply chain milestones.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:58.340
The drying surface through standard patent processes without prior official announcement.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.480
A former Tesla executive has launched a company to produce the residential heat pump

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:09.700
previously discussed by Elon Musk. The product targets home energy efficiency and integration

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:16.140
with solar and storage systems. Development continues after Tesla's own heat pump program paused.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:22.580
Early prototypes focus on cost and installation simplicity. Market entry timing will depend

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:28.820
on supply chain and certification progress. The new venture seeks to deliver hardware that aligns

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:35.460
with residential solar ecosystems already in widespread use. The three companies are scaling a joint

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:41.980
robotaxi effort across multiple continents. Stellantis vehicles will integrate wave autonomy

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:48.260
software under Uber's ride hailing network. The alliance aims to accelerate deployment beyond single

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:55.540
market tests. Initial operations will focus on controlled urban corridors. Expansion plans include

00:09:55.540 --> 00:10:02.020
coordinated regulatory filings in several jurisdictions. The partnership structure combines vehicle

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:09.000
manufacturing scale with established ride hailing infrastructure. A pilot program places vacuums

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:14.620
at certain charging locations for quick interior cleaning. Owners can use the equipment while the

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:20.840
vehicle charges. The amenity targets short dwell times during road trips. Early sites are being

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:27.600
evaluated for usage and maintenance needs. Feedback from initial locations will guide decisions on wider

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:33.640
rollout. The addition provides a practical service that aligns with typical supercharger stop durations.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:40.000
Before we go, keep an eye on how the Taiwan filing and the upcoming software features interact

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:47.940
once regulators begin their review. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news. TSLA closed at 398

